509
00:22:09.780 --> 00:22:10.700
I saw a picture of it.

510
00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:10.900
Okay.

511
00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:12.020
Here's how it worked.

512
00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:15.360
Since every call was connected manually, you know, by a...

513
00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:16.300
Oh, you didn't dial a number.

514
00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:16.740
No.

515
00:22:16.900 --> 00:22:22.280
You were connected by a central switchboard operator, and the subscriber list was so small,

516
00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:23.560
no numbers were necessary.

517
00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:24.080
Sure.

518
00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:28.120
You would just dial up the person, the switchboard, and you'd be like...

519
00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:29.160
Connect me to...

520
00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:30.100
...to whoever.

521
00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:30.700
Right.

522
00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:34.260
Yeah, Angela Kinsey, if you were in the pamphlet, I'd know you have a phone.

523
00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:34.820
That's right.

524
00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:35.500
Huh.

525
00:22:35.800 --> 00:22:41.220
What's amazing is this company grew and went through many different configurations, but

526
00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:46.100
it provided independent telecommunication service to the state of Connecticut until 1998.

527
00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:47.160
Wow.

528
00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:47.960
I know.

529
00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:52.380
I love reading about the origin of things, but it also reminded me of a simpler time.

530
00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:59.340
And when I moved to Archer City, Texas, I would ask for people's phone numbers, and

531
00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:00.700
they would just give you four digits.

532
00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:03.320
Because the first ones were all the same?

533
00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:03.960
Yes.

534
00:23:04.080 --> 00:23:05.300
And the town was so small.

535
00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:10.960
So I moved from Indonesia, you know, and then I moved to this small town, and I thought

536
00:23:10.960 --> 00:23:12.200
everyone just had four numbers.

537
00:23:12.760 --> 00:23:13.580
That's so funny.

538
00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:16.660
And when I went to college, I would be like, what are your four numbers?

539
00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:18.580
I know.

540
00:23:18.720 --> 00:23:20.020
It's just crazy to think about.

541
00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:22.340
People were like, don't you need all of them, Ange?

542
00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:23.520
I'm like, no, I just need four.

543
00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:24.140
And they're like, nope.

544
00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:24.880
Just need the last four.

545
00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:25.200
Nope.

546
00:23:25.560 --> 00:23:27.000
Do you remember 411?

547
00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:28.020
Yes.

548
00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:29.340
Is that still a thing?

549
00:23:29.940 --> 00:23:36.820
Like you used to call up 411 and be like, I'm looking for the phone number of something

550
00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:38.600
like Lewis's tires.

551
00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:39.480
I don't know.

552
00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:40.260
Should we call it?

553
00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:41.100
Sure.

554
00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:41.920
I mean, I'm scared.

555
00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:44.500
What happens when you dial 411 now?

556
00:23:44.660 --> 00:23:45.300
Let's not be scared.

557
00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:45.540
Let's see.

558
00:23:45.540 --> 00:23:46.640
Well, what are we going to ask for?

559
00:23:47.160 --> 00:23:48.720
Ask for Pizza Hut.

560
00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:49.120
Okay.

561
00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:55.510
The service you are calling is not available from this location.

562
00:23:55.670 --> 00:23:56.050
Oh.

563
00:23:56.090 --> 00:23:57.170
If this is an emergency.

564
00:23:57.490 --> 00:23:57.830
Oh.

565
00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:00.350
Well, we'll never get Pizza Hut now.

566
00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:00.790
Nope.

567
00:24:01.230 --> 00:24:03.330
I'm just going to go without pizza today, I guess.

568
00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:05.230
Now you have me hungry for pizza.

569
00:24:05.410 --> 00:24:05.690
Sorry.

570
00:24:06.310 --> 00:24:07.270
Well, there you go.

571
00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:09.530
A little bit of the origin of the first phone book.

572
00:24:09.690 --> 00:24:11.570
The first phone book would not have been a whale.

573
00:24:11.870 --> 00:24:14.230
It would have been like a little, like a minnow.

574
00:24:15.090 --> 00:24:15.470
Yes.

575
00:24:16.150 --> 00:24:21.510
Also during this phone call with David Wallace, Dwight asks if Tom Peterman is still in charge

576
00:24:21.510 --> 00:24:22.670
of the White Pages account.

577
00:24:23.370 --> 00:24:24.770
We find out, no.

578
00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:28.650
It is now run by a woman, but David doesn't know her name.

579
00:24:29.130 --> 00:24:30.750
Phyllis immediately perks up.

580
00:24:30.870 --> 00:24:31.750
She's like, no, no, no.

581
00:24:31.970 --> 00:24:33.610
Dwight cannot handle this sale.

582
00:24:33.790 --> 00:24:35.190
He is horrible with women.

583
00:24:35.470 --> 00:24:35.850
Yes.

584
00:24:35.850 --> 00:24:37.990
He kept calling Gina Rogers Gina.

585
00:24:38.430 --> 00:24:38.990
Yes.

586
00:24:39.270 --> 00:24:42.010
She said she had to correct him five times.

587
00:24:42.310 --> 00:24:43.930
Dwight says, Gina said that?

588
00:24:44.230 --> 00:24:45.990
The scene was actually longer.

589
00:24:45.990 --> 00:24:51.490
And in the shooting draft, Dwight then turns to Angela and asks her, did I ever make you

590
00:24:51.490 --> 00:24:52.070
feel uncomfortable?

591
00:24:52.570 --> 00:24:53.710
This is how it read.

592
00:24:54.330 --> 00:24:55.530
Dwight, false.

593
00:24:55.910 --> 00:24:59.610
Angela, did I make you uncomfortable when I'd have sex with you in the warehouse?

594
00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:01.590
Angela, quickly for camera.

595
00:25:01.910 --> 00:25:05.290
I was a virgin before marriage and I have never set foot in a warehouse.

596
00:25:06.490 --> 00:25:11.690
So they let us do a bunch of takes and in one we improvised and it made it into deleted

597
00:25:11.690 --> 00:25:12.150
scenes.

598
00:25:12.370 --> 00:25:13.170
I want you to hear it.

599
00:25:13.770 --> 00:25:15.710
Dwight, you make women feel uncomfortable.

600
00:25:15.990 --> 00:25:17.170
That, ah, come on.

601
00:25:17.370 --> 00:25:18.330
That is so not true.

602
00:25:18.490 --> 00:25:23.710
Angela, when we would have meetings in the warehouse, did I make you feel uncomfortable?

603
00:25:24.550 --> 00:25:26.690
Uh, those meetings were very brief.

604
00:25:27.930 --> 00:25:28.950
Boring, even.

605
00:25:29.770 --> 00:25:31.210
I remember them being...

606
00:25:31.210 --> 00:25:32.030
Well, they weren't.

607
00:25:33.390 --> 00:25:35.510
Oh, Angela, that is so funny.

608
00:25:35.770 --> 00:25:36.170
I know.

609
00:25:36.210 --> 00:25:37.410
That is such a good improv.

610
00:25:37.430 --> 00:25:40.290
It was so fun when I was like, it was very brief.

611
00:25:41.330 --> 00:25:43.950
Rain's face as Dwight was like, hey.

612
00:25:46.810 --> 00:25:49.590
Well, Phyllis is not going to let this go, you guys.

613
00:25:49.750 --> 00:25:55.370
She's like, listen, an account this size could double their gross, you know, their salaries,

614
00:25:55.550 --> 00:25:56.050
their bonuses.

615
00:25:56.290 --> 00:25:57.890
Pizza Friday could come back.

616
00:25:58.270 --> 00:26:00.390
They're not going to be able to call Pizza Hut, though.

617
00:26:00.710 --> 00:26:01.770
Not with 411.

618
00:26:01.970 --> 00:26:02.530
No, they're not.

619
00:26:03.090 --> 00:26:05.250
Pam says, Jim, can you go instead?

620
00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:06.610
But he can't.

621
00:26:06.770 --> 00:26:11.470
He has his first board meeting conference call for his new business.

622
00:26:11.470 --> 00:26:11.910
Yeah.

623
00:26:12.170 --> 00:26:12.570
Yeah.

624
00:26:12.850 --> 00:26:14.610
So, he's busy.

625
00:26:15.430 --> 00:26:17.210
Dwight's going to run point on this.

626
00:26:17.330 --> 00:26:17.830
Oh, no.

627
00:26:17.990 --> 00:26:18.590
Buckle in.

628
00:26:19.570 --> 00:26:23.190
Meanwhile, we have this whole other storyline that really cracked me up.

629
00:26:23.270 --> 00:26:24.170
We talked about it.

630
00:26:24.730 --> 00:26:25.170
Movember.

631
00:26:25.610 --> 00:26:27.310
Pete is going to enter the break room.

632
00:26:27.430 --> 00:26:29.010
I don't even know what you would title this.

633
00:26:29.230 --> 00:26:30.430
Stashy in the break room?

634
00:26:30.550 --> 00:26:31.270
I guess so.

635
00:26:31.670 --> 00:26:32.830
Mustache in the break room.

636
00:26:33.050 --> 00:26:34.010
Mustache in the break room.

637
00:26:34.190 --> 00:26:37.150
He's got a little mustache, and so do Daryl, Clark, and Kevin.

638
00:26:37.270 --> 00:26:38.610
They're all very unshaven.

639
00:26:38.610 --> 00:26:42.710
And Pete and Clark have a joint talking head where they say Toby got them to participate

640
00:26:42.710 --> 00:26:46.170
in Movember, and they're going to have mustaches the whole month.

641
00:26:46.430 --> 00:26:49.270
So, you know, hope you like being turned on all the time.

642
00:26:49.610 --> 00:26:52.330
Toby enters, and he has a very—

643
00:26:52.330 --> 00:26:53.850
I don't even know what you call it.

644
00:26:53.930 --> 00:26:54.530
It's a—

645
00:26:54.530 --> 00:26:55.250
It's a squirrel.

646
00:26:55.490 --> 00:26:56.430
It's a squirrel tail.

647
00:26:56.770 --> 00:26:58.070
He's very proud.

648
00:26:58.070 --> 00:27:02.130
He can clearly grow a mustache, a very hearty mustache.

649
00:27:02.130 --> 00:27:09.550
When he—when Paul walked on set with that, I remember losing it because it was so wispy

650
00:27:09.550 --> 00:27:12.470
and weird, and it hung down on his chin.

651
00:27:12.770 --> 00:27:17.230
I want you to know, lady, when Toby says that he has very fertile hair glands—

652
00:27:17.750 --> 00:27:18.130
Yes.

653
00:27:19.630 --> 00:27:20.790
I Googled that.

654
00:27:20.890 --> 00:27:22.070
I wondered if it was a thing.

655
00:27:22.310 --> 00:27:22.710
Oh.

656
00:27:22.930 --> 00:27:24.090
Fertile hair glands.

657
00:27:24.310 --> 00:27:24.470
Yeah.

658
00:27:24.790 --> 00:27:29.330
Do you want to know the very first thing that comes up when you just type in fertile

659
00:27:29.330 --> 00:27:30.450
hair glands?

660
00:27:30.930 --> 00:27:31.510
Do I?

661
00:27:31.510 --> 00:27:32.550
Do I?

662
00:27:32.550 --> 00:27:32.690
Do I?

663
00:27:32.970 --> 00:27:35.410
It's a photo of Toby.

664
00:27:35.710 --> 00:27:35.970
No!

665
00:27:36.510 --> 00:27:36.950
Yep.

666
00:27:36.950 --> 00:27:38.950
It's the very first thing that comes up.

667
00:27:39.190 --> 00:27:41.310
I didn't feel like I had to go any further than that.

668
00:27:41.430 --> 00:27:41.630
Okay.

669
00:27:41.630 --> 00:27:42.690
Because that was amazing.

670
00:27:43.030 --> 00:27:48.830
Paul Lieberstein, just so you know, on Google, if you type in fertile hair glands, a photo

671
00:27:48.830 --> 00:27:49.970
of you comes up.

672
00:27:50.590 --> 00:27:51.950
That is pretty incredible.

673
00:27:52.270 --> 00:27:56.690
Well, Toby is so delighted that these guys have participated in Movember.

674
00:27:56.790 --> 00:27:59.010
Well, because he's got a buddy group now.

675
00:27:59.010 --> 00:27:59.370
Yes.

676
00:27:59.370 --> 00:28:00.990
They're bonded over their mustaches.

677
00:28:00.990 --> 00:28:03.130
And they're all back in the annex hanging out.

678
00:28:03.370 --> 00:28:04.330
They go to lunch.

679
00:28:04.410 --> 00:28:05.510
They do stuff together.

680
00:28:05.790 --> 00:28:06.450
They're hanging out.

681
00:28:06.930 --> 00:28:11.310
The scene was longer, and Creed is going to share about a time he grew a mustache.

682
00:28:11.590 --> 00:28:12.810
I think we should hear it.

683
00:28:12.810 --> 00:28:14.390
I had a mustache once.

684
00:28:14.850 --> 00:28:16.850
My lady friends called it the tickler.

685
00:28:17.490 --> 00:28:19.130
They stick it right in their armpits.

686
00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:24.320
Well, I'm going to say that was a good edit.

687
00:28:24.580 --> 00:28:28.040
That they took out Creed saying his lady friends called him the tickler?

688
00:28:28.160 --> 00:28:28.620
Yes.

689
00:28:28.620 --> 00:28:30.780
Oh, it cracked me up.

690
00:28:31.060 --> 00:28:33.900
Well, I'll tell you what cracked me up this next scene.

691
00:28:34.380 --> 00:28:34.760
Oh.

692
00:28:34.760 --> 00:28:36.960
This is one of my favorites.

693
00:28:37.520 --> 00:28:39.400
Oscar is doing some fall cleaning.

694
00:28:39.760 --> 00:28:41.640
He's cleaning out his desk drawer.

695
00:28:41.860 --> 00:28:45.980
I want you to know every single bit about that desk drawer was scripted.

696
00:28:45.980 --> 00:28:46.920
I know.

697
00:28:47.100 --> 00:28:47.880
I looked it up.

698
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:50.620
I was like, what was this bit?

699
00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:51.760
All of it.

700
00:28:51.880 --> 00:28:52.400
The whole thing.

701
00:28:52.540 --> 00:28:53.880
All the details were scripted.

702
00:28:54.400 --> 00:28:59.180
He's cleaning out this drawer, and Angela says, I think the senator is having an affair,

703
00:28:59.360 --> 00:29:02.720
and the drawer comes unhinged in his hands.

704
00:29:03.080 --> 00:29:04.380
It is so good.

705
00:29:04.380 --> 00:29:08.260
And you know when that happens, it's like, you can't get it back in there.

706
00:29:08.380 --> 00:29:08.620
No.

707
00:29:09.040 --> 00:29:09.300
No.

708
00:29:09.900 --> 00:29:12.420
Carrie Kemper said this is her favorite scene.

709
00:29:12.680 --> 00:29:15.220
She said she originally scripted it a little differently.

710
00:29:15.520 --> 00:29:19.880
She said it was originally scripted in the kitchen, and Oscar was going to be toasting

711
00:29:19.880 --> 00:29:24.060
some bread, and you were going to come in and say, I think the senator is cheating on

712
00:29:24.060 --> 00:29:30.200
me, and he was going to accidentally knock the toast lever up, and the toast was going

713
00:29:30.200 --> 00:29:33.140
to go flying in the air, and he was going to, like, swat at the toaSt.

714
00:29:33.800 --> 00:29:35.140
She said it was a little much.

715
00:29:35.280 --> 00:29:41.140
It got changed to the desk drawer gag, but she said she just loved seeing Oscar do physical

716
00:29:41.140 --> 00:29:45.900
comedy, and she really, she still kind of wishes that she would have gotten her toast

717
00:29:45.900 --> 00:29:49.420
gag because she thinks Oscar would have killed it, and she wanted to see your reaction of

718
00:29:49.420 --> 00:29:50.600
him, like, swatting toaSt.

719
00:29:50.900 --> 00:29:52.320
It was just so funny.

720
00:29:52.460 --> 00:29:54.340
I can't even imagine him swatting toaSt.

721
00:29:54.460 --> 00:29:55.700
I wouldn't have been able to get through it.

722
00:29:58.180 --> 00:30:02.680
Also, Oscar feigning surprise or any emotion like that.

723
00:30:03.140 --> 00:30:04.500
Is just, he's brilliant.

724
00:30:04.820 --> 00:30:06.100
He's such a good actor.

725
00:30:06.380 --> 00:30:08.820
This cuts to a talking head with Oscar.

726
00:30:09.040 --> 00:30:14.540
He shares that he has had nightmares about this exact scenario, and he wakes up in a sweat

727
00:30:14.540 --> 00:30:16.960
and makes Angela's husband spoon him back to bed.

728
00:30:16.960 --> 00:30:17.620
Mm-hmm.

729
00:30:17.800 --> 00:30:21.040
Well, there was actually one more scripted line after that line.

730
00:30:21.260 --> 00:30:24.540
It's in the shooting draft, and I thought I'd read it to you.

731
00:30:24.700 --> 00:30:25.040
All right.

732
00:30:25.800 --> 00:30:30.960
After he says, I would make Angela's husband spoon me back to bed, he would then look ashamed

733
00:30:30.960 --> 00:30:34.160
and then look at camera and say, I'm one cold mother******.

734
00:30:36.880 --> 00:30:38.940
There was also a candy bag alt.

735
00:30:39.060 --> 00:30:41.020
It was a must shoot, so we did shoot it.

736
00:30:41.020 --> 00:30:46.200
But Oscar would have said, I have nightmares in which Angela walks in on the senator and me.

737
00:30:46.340 --> 00:30:48.900
I also have nightmares in which Angela and I have lunch.

738
00:30:49.080 --> 00:30:49.720
It's weird.

739
00:30:50.080 --> 00:30:51.420
Angela's in all my nightmares.

740
00:30:52.180 --> 00:30:53.640
I kind of love that.

741
00:30:53.780 --> 00:30:54.600
I did too.

742
00:30:55.120 --> 00:30:58.460
I love that the idea of the two of them having lunch is a nightmare.

743
00:30:58.880 --> 00:31:06.280
Well, Angela confides in Oscar that the senator has a secret little smile on his face when he

744
00:31:06.280 --> 00:31:07.340
comes home in the morning.

745
00:31:07.340 --> 00:31:09.520
And Oscar makes a noise like, aw.

746
00:31:10.860 --> 00:31:15.720
And also, she says, the senator is always at this yoga studio.

747
00:31:15.960 --> 00:31:16.160
Yeah.

748
00:31:16.300 --> 00:31:19.320
He never misses noon hot yoga with Blake.

749
00:31:19.760 --> 00:31:22.560
And Oscar's like, you have nothing to worry about.

750
00:31:22.900 --> 00:31:28.480
Blake is also a guy's name, so he could be spending the day wait with the guy wait a second.

751
00:31:28.980 --> 00:31:29.360
Yes.

752
00:31:29.520 --> 00:31:31.540
And then Oscar's like, who is this Blake?

753
00:31:31.820 --> 00:31:32.780
And Angela's like, yeah.

754
00:31:32.780 --> 00:31:32.840
Yeah.

755
00:31:33.240 --> 00:31:37.500
And Oscar's like, I never heard anything about the senator doing yoga, you know, from you.

756
00:31:37.660 --> 00:31:38.520
And I'm like, right?

757
00:31:39.140 --> 00:31:40.260
What's with all the yoga?

758
00:31:40.600 --> 00:31:40.960
Exactly.

759
00:31:41.500 --> 00:31:43.320
And then Oscar's like, okay, calm down.

760
00:31:43.480 --> 00:31:44.860
But we have to check this out.

761
00:31:44.980 --> 00:31:45.840
And Angela's like, what?

762
00:31:46.320 --> 00:31:46.620
Yeah.

763
00:31:46.720 --> 00:31:47.680
He's like, I'll go with you.

764
00:31:48.100 --> 00:31:49.860
I loved every second of this scene.

765
00:31:50.080 --> 00:31:50.400
It's delicious.

766
00:31:50.480 --> 00:31:51.320
It's so good.

767
00:31:51.720 --> 00:31:55.380
I always thought a really fun spinoff would be Angela and Oscar being roommates.

768
00:31:55.680 --> 00:31:58.120
You know, when Angela moves in with him, we're not there yet.

769
00:31:58.120 --> 00:32:02.840
But I remember telling Greg, if I could see anything more of this show, it'd be Angela

770
