That's what you're basically saying.

1275
00:52:54.700 --> 00:52:55.480
I'm very sorry.

1276
00:52:55.740 --> 00:52:55.790
Right?

1277
00:52:55.790 --> 00:52:56.420
I am.

1278
00:52:56.420 --> 00:52:57.560
I mean, is that it, Pam?

1279
00:52:57.740 --> 00:52:58.040
No.

1280
00:52:58.220 --> 00:52:58.460
That's.

1281
00:52:58.640 --> 00:52:58.920
I'm.

1282
00:52:59.120 --> 00:52:59.820
I'm sorry.

1283
00:52:59.820 --> 00:53:00.240
No, I hear it.

1284
00:53:00.380 --> 00:53:01.100
I hear it.

1285
00:53:01.820 --> 00:53:03.520
Do you have another one of these?

1286
00:53:04.440 --> 00:53:05.320
The slideshows?

1287
00:53:05.540 --> 00:53:06.360
Let's see it.

1288
00:53:06.520 --> 00:53:06.820
Molly!

1289
00:53:08.580 --> 00:53:09.560
Oh, my goodness.

1290
00:53:10.560 --> 00:53:11.940
Jan is so unpredictable.

1291
00:53:12.260 --> 00:53:14.960
Pam is just trying to, like, have a conversation.

1292
00:53:15.160 --> 00:53:16.360
Are you saying I'm unlovable?

1293
00:53:16.640 --> 00:53:18.060
Like, wait, how do we get there?

1294
00:53:18.180 --> 00:53:20.860
But she's also, like, trying to defend herself.

1295
00:53:21.180 --> 00:53:23.360
Because Jan is insulting her.

1296
00:53:23.560 --> 00:53:24.060
I know.

1297
00:53:24.260 --> 00:53:25.020
Oh, my goodness.

1298
00:53:25.020 --> 00:53:29.060
I also feel like we have to talk about the slideshow and the song.

1299
00:53:29.500 --> 00:53:32.640
And this is the last time we're going to hear Jan sing.

1300
00:53:32.960 --> 00:53:33.400
Yes.

1301
00:53:33.600 --> 00:53:34.620
And we need to hear it.

1302
00:53:34.900 --> 00:53:35.180
Okay.

1303
00:53:36.860 --> 00:53:38.820
Mommy, you're a princess.

1304
00:53:55.460 --> 00:53:55.980
Wow.

1305
00:53:57.340 --> 00:53:58.460
Wow is right.

1306
00:53:58.820 --> 00:53:59.340
Wow.

1307
00:53:59.600 --> 00:54:01.160
That's the only response to that.

1308
00:54:01.360 --> 00:54:01.880
Wow.

1309
00:54:02.120 --> 00:54:02.520
Wow.

1310
00:54:02.880 --> 00:54:03.780
Oh, Melora.

1311
00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:05.260
Amazing, amazing job.

1312
00:54:05.820 --> 00:54:08.820
Well, there's a little flirty at reception happening.

1313
00:54:09.360 --> 00:54:10.340
There is.

1314
00:54:10.540 --> 00:54:14.300
Pete is trying to talk to Erin, but she's very grossed out by his mustache.

1315
00:54:14.640 --> 00:54:17.320
Here's a list of all the insults Erin says to Pete.

1316
00:54:17.320 --> 00:54:19.240
I mean, she says them nicely.

1317
00:54:19.560 --> 00:54:22.480
She says, there's an eyebrow in the middle of your face.

1318
00:54:22.900 --> 00:54:28.560
She says, your handsome eyebrow makes it look like your mouth is like an eye socket.

1319
00:54:28.800 --> 00:54:32.280
She also says he looks like a cyclops, but whose eye fell out.

1320
00:54:32.720 --> 00:54:36.380
And Pete immediately goes and shaves off the mustache.

1321
00:54:36.600 --> 00:54:37.200
Yes, exactly.

1322
00:54:38.100 --> 00:54:39.760
Movember is over now for Pete.

1323
00:54:40.440 --> 00:54:45.000
Back at the yoga studio, Oscar and Angela continue to spy on the senator.

1324
00:54:46.560 --> 00:54:54.580
And Oscar suggests that maybe the affair that Angela should be worried about is with this man.

1325
00:54:55.080 --> 00:54:55.300
Yeah.

1326
00:54:55.740 --> 00:54:57.560
Angela's like, Oscar, what is happening here?

1327
00:54:57.620 --> 00:55:00.100
Why would you say you think the senator might be gay?

1328
00:55:00.380 --> 00:55:05.000
And I loved Oscar's performance here when he says, I don't know, Angela, I'm dehydrated.

1329
00:55:05.180 --> 00:55:06.320
Maybe you heard me wrong.

1330
00:55:06.420 --> 00:55:07.120
We should just go.

1331
00:55:07.340 --> 00:55:09.000
And then Angela's like, oh, here he comes.

1332
00:55:09.020 --> 00:55:09.520
What's he doing?

1333
00:55:09.520 --> 00:55:11.440
And Oscar says he's making a phone call.

1334
00:55:11.900 --> 00:55:14.440
And then Oscar's phone rings.

1335
00:55:14.760 --> 00:55:18.460
This is how the stage direction was written for this moment in the shooting draft.

1336
00:55:19.420 --> 00:55:21.100
Suddenly, Oscar's phone rings.

1337
00:55:21.380 --> 00:55:22.460
Angela looks at the phone.

1338
00:55:22.960 --> 00:55:25.300
Oscar fumbles with it, trying to turn it off.

1339
00:55:25.540 --> 00:55:28.980
Angela looks from Oscar to the senator and back.

1340
00:55:29.580 --> 00:55:31.440
Oscar looks at her guiltily.

1341
00:55:31.720 --> 00:55:34.180
She reads it in his face and knows.

1342
00:55:34.680 --> 00:55:35.880
Very interesting.

1343
00:55:35.880 --> 00:55:37.020
That all played out.

1344
00:55:37.020 --> 00:55:39.980
I mean, I saw all of that play out in your scene.

1345
00:55:40.680 --> 00:55:43.080
Well, you know, we filmed this scene multiple times.

1346
00:55:43.240 --> 00:55:51.760
They kept moving the camera around because they really wanted to make sure that they could capture Oscar and I looking at each other, but that we were also hidden from the senator,

1347
00:55:51.940 --> 00:55:53.520
but that the camera could see the senator.

1348
00:55:53.520 --> 00:56:00.100
So they kept moving the camera around, and I actually have all of the unedited takes from this moment.

1349
00:56:00.520 --> 00:56:00.800
Really?

1350
00:56:00.800 --> 00:56:01.340
Yeah.

1351
00:56:01.560 --> 00:56:03.400
They were given to me way back when.

1352
00:56:03.560 --> 00:56:06.820
I found him in my digital clutter, and I have all of them.

1353
00:56:06.940 --> 00:56:09.120
The moment the phone rings and I look at him.

1354
00:56:09.340 --> 00:56:17.920
In some takes, they had me grab my coat and walk off in a huff, and then other takes, they just had me hold this stare at him, and that's what they used.

1355
00:56:18.480 --> 00:56:18.820
Wow.

1356
00:56:19.160 --> 00:56:20.140
Well, it's really funny.

1357
00:56:20.240 --> 00:56:25.540
When I was watching this episode and I saw these scenes, I was like, why do I feel like I was there?

1358
00:56:25.760 --> 00:56:26.660
This was a location.

1359
00:56:26.660 --> 00:56:27.800
I wouldn't have been there.

1360
00:56:27.900 --> 00:56:30.000
But, Angela, I was.

1361
00:56:30.180 --> 00:56:31.080
I was.

1362
00:56:31.320 --> 00:56:38.140
Steve Burgess reminded me that we shot this yoga studio at the 360 Health Club in Reseda, California.

1363
00:56:38.700 --> 00:56:41.880
In the morning, we shot in the parking lot.

1364
00:56:42.020 --> 00:56:44.860
We shot that scene of me and Dwight out in the car.

1365
00:56:45.080 --> 00:56:54.600
And we did all of our driving scenes around this area, and I came in, and I said hi to you guys because they were setting up your interior work.

1366
00:56:55.000 --> 00:56:56.420
So I was there.

1367
00:56:56.740 --> 00:56:57.700
Oh, my gosh.

1368
00:56:57.980 --> 00:56:58.240
I know.

1369
00:56:58.360 --> 00:56:59.260
I totally remember it.

1370
00:56:59.300 --> 00:57:02.760
Our base camp was in the parking lot, and so I was there that day.

1371
00:57:02.760 --> 00:57:03.500
I remember.

1372
00:57:03.720 --> 00:57:05.120
And I love those scenes.

1373
00:57:05.360 --> 00:57:05.800
Thank you.

1374
00:57:05.800 --> 00:57:08.400
I absolutely love them, and I loved rewatching them.

1375
00:57:08.580 --> 00:57:11.420
And I want to call Oscar and be like, Oscar, let's do a show.

1376
00:57:11.860 --> 00:57:12.620
You should.

1377
00:57:13.300 --> 00:57:17.220
Well, Dwight is now going to come back to Jan's office, and guess who he has in tow?

1378
00:57:18.140 --> 00:57:18.540
Clark.

1379
00:57:19.000 --> 00:57:19.400
Clark.

1380
00:57:19.820 --> 00:57:21.820
Clark, like as a token?

1381
00:57:22.060 --> 00:57:24.540
Like, Dwight is offering up Clark to Jan?

1382
00:57:24.560 --> 00:57:25.460
What the heck?

1383
00:57:25.640 --> 00:57:28.260
Well, he says Molly is a crap assistant.

1384
00:57:28.700 --> 00:57:29.920
You can have Clark.

1385
00:57:30.160 --> 00:57:30.420
Yeah.

1386
00:57:30.820 --> 00:57:31.540
How about that?

1387
00:57:31.740 --> 00:57:33.340
Pam's like, Clark, you don't have to do this.

1388
00:57:33.420 --> 00:57:34.520
And he goes, no, I want to get ahead.

1389
00:57:34.520 --> 00:57:36.600
I want to get ahead in the paper sale industry.

1390
00:57:36.840 --> 00:57:39.860
Do you know why the storyline was in place?

1391
00:57:40.160 --> 00:57:41.880
Where was Clark in real life going?

1392
00:57:42.040 --> 00:57:42.780
Had he booked a movie?

1393
00:57:42.780 --> 00:57:43.860
Yes, he had.

1394
00:57:44.160 --> 00:57:46.760
Clark needed time off to go film Kick-Ass 2.

1395
00:57:47.260 --> 00:57:52.020
So we put Ed on a boat because he was off filming Hangover 3.

1396
00:57:52.200 --> 00:57:56.080
We gave Clark to Jan because he had to film Kick-Ass 2.

1397
00:57:56.500 --> 00:58:02.240
Also, after we shot this episode, we took a three-week hiatus to give these gentlemen a

1398
00:58:02.240 --> 00:58:04.160
little bit more time to do their movies.

1399
00:58:04.540 --> 00:58:04.980
Oh.

1400
00:58:05.720 --> 00:58:05.880
Hmm.

1401
00:58:06.520 --> 00:58:07.100
Well, that is—

1402
00:58:07.100 --> 00:58:07.520
Did you hear that?

1403
00:58:07.580 --> 00:58:16.600
It's exactly one year ago at the same time that I was asking for maternity leave.

1404
00:58:16.720 --> 00:58:17.100
Correct.

1405
00:58:17.280 --> 00:58:17.480
Yes.

1406
00:58:17.480 --> 00:58:19.300
And I was told we can't do that.

1407
00:58:19.420 --> 00:58:19.740
No.

1408
00:58:19.740 --> 00:58:25.900
We can't take a three-week break so that you can heal from birthing a human.

1409
00:58:26.320 --> 00:58:26.680
Yeah.

1410
00:58:26.860 --> 00:58:27.740
We couldn't do that.

1411
00:58:27.900 --> 00:58:34.400
We'd done it all the other years for movie projects, seasons one through seven, and then

1412
00:58:34.400 --> 00:58:36.020
again here in season nine.

1413
00:58:36.020 --> 00:58:40.780
But apparently in season eight, we just couldn't.

1414
00:58:41.240 --> 00:58:41.980
You know what?

1415
00:58:42.100 --> 00:58:43.580
You should have been in Kick-Ass 3.

1416
00:58:44.060 --> 00:58:48.320
Maybe if I'd done Blades of Glory 2, I could have had three weeks off.

1417
00:58:48.560 --> 00:58:50.240
I don't know what Kick-Ass is.

1418
00:58:50.720 --> 00:58:52.080
I don't know Kick-Ass 1.

1419
